<p><strong>My daily driver is a MacBook Pro M3 Pro.</strong> I grade 4K BRAW and ProRes 422 HQ footage from my BMPCC 6K Pro and Sony FX3 on it daily. Resolve runs smoother on this than on my old desktop with an RTX 3070. The unified memory architecture means 18 GB of "RAM" is shared between CPU and GPU — so Resolve gets to use all of it as VRAM. No other laptop does this at this price.</p>

<p>If you're on Windows and need raw GPU power for heavy Fusion work or 8K footage, the RTX 4070 laptops in this range are excellent. But they run hot, have 2-3 hour battery life, and weigh 2.5 kg — keep that in mind if you edit on location.</p>

